00:11:09.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Craig Anderson had lived in Jackson, Mississippi for most of his adult life. He was originally from Holmes County and was primarily raised by his mother after his father died. Craig was one of four children with an older sister and two younger brothers. He grew up to become a kind and courteous person who was particularly caring towards children and the elderly. His defining feature was what his sister Barbara called his grand piano smile. As a young man, Craig moved 70 miles south to Jackson, where in 1993, at the age of 30, he was introduced to James, another African-American man. James later told journalist Albert Samaha from BuzzFeed News that by the end of their first day, the pair had fallen for one another. The cautious and organized the James kept Craig in check, while Craig's warm and easygoing personality allowed James to loosen up a little.
克雷格·安德森在密西西比州杰克逊市度过了他成年后的大部分时光。他原籍霍姆斯县，父亲去世后主要由母亲抚养长大。克雷格是四个孩子中的一个，有一个姐姐和两个弟弟。他长大后成为一个善良、有礼貌的人，尤其关心儿童和老人。他最显著的特征是他姐姐芭芭拉所说的“三角钢琴般的微笑”。年轻时，克雷格向南搬了70英里来到杰克逊，1993年，30岁的他在那里经人介绍认识了另一名非裔美国人詹姆斯。詹姆斯后来对《BuzzFeed新闻》的记者阿尔伯特·萨马哈说，在他们相识的第一天结束时，两人就已经坠入爱河。谨慎而有条理的詹姆斯管束着克雷格，而克雷格温暖随和的性格让詹姆斯得以放松一些。

10
00:12:18.000 --> 00:13:37.000
On a number of occasions, James surprised Craig with trips to cities like Chicago, New Orleans, and Miami. There, the couple were more comfortable being affectionate in public, unlike in Jackson, where members of the LGBTQI community often faced discrimination. Five years into their relationship, James and Craig bought a house in Jackson. James wasn't initially keen on the property as he thought it was ugly, but Craig saw its potential and spent the next few years turning it into a home. He put in new flooring, painted the walls, renovated the kitchen, and planted a garden full of flowers. Craig also picked out all of the furniture and decorated the house with plush green carpet and paintings of tigers. The couple were active churchgoers at the first Hyde Park Missionary Baptist Church, where Craig sang as tenor in the choir. By 2004, Craig and James had been together for 11 years and knew they wanted to spend the rest of their lives together.
在多次场合中，詹姆斯用去芝加哥、新奥尔良和迈阿密等城市的旅行给克雷格带来惊喜。在那里，这对情侣更习惯在公共场合表现出亲密感，而不像在杰克逊，LGBTQI社群的成员经常面临歧视。交往五年后，詹姆斯和克雷格在杰克逊买了一栋房子。詹姆斯起初并不喜欢这处房产，因为他觉得它很丑，但克雷格看到了它的潜力，并在接下来的几年里把它变成了一个家。他铺设了新地板，粉刷了墙壁，翻新了厨房，并种满了鲜花。克雷格还挑选了所有的家具，用毛绒绿地毯和老虎画装点房子。这对夫妇是海德公园第一传教士浸信会教堂的积极礼拜者，克雷格在唱诗班里担任男高音。到2004年，克雷格和詹姆斯已经在一起11年了，他们知道自己想要共度余生。

11
00:13:37.000 --> 00:14:53.000
At the time, Mississippi didn't recognize same-sex marriage, so they held a private ceremony in New Orleans, where they exchanged vows and rings. Months later, Craig was offered a job as a production technician at a Nissan vehicle manufacturing plant in Canton, roughly 20 miles north of Jackson. Craig was thrilled as the position was higher paid than his previous job, and James later told BuzzFeed News that he'd reacted by, quote, jumping around, smiling like it was the best day of his life. The couple celebrated with a trip to Memphis, Tennessee. In 2007, a situation arose within James' extended family that resulted in a relative needing to re-home their newborn baby boy. James was eager to adopt, but Craig wasn't sure they were ready for the responsibility. They decided to proceed with the adoption, and Craig immediately embraced the role of a devoted father. He loved spoiling their adopted son with chocolates and toys.
当时，密西西比州不承认同性婚姻，因此他们在纽奥良举行了一场私人仪式，在那里他们交换了誓言和戒指。几个月后，克雷格获得了一份工作，担任位于杰克逊以北约20英里坎顿的日产汽车制造厂的生产技术员。克雷格欣喜若狂，因为这个职位的薪水比他以前的工作要高，詹姆斯后来告诉《BuzzFeed新闻》，他的反应是“跳来跳去，笑得就像那是他生命中最美好的一天”。这对夫妇去田纳西州孟菲斯旅行来庆祝。2007年，詹姆斯的大家庭中出现了一种情况，导致一位亲戚需要为他们刚出生的男婴重新安置家庭。詹姆斯渴望收养，但克雷格不确定他们是否准备好承担这个责任。他们决定继续进行收养，克雷格立即扮演了一个慈爱父亲的角色。他喜欢用巧克力和玩具宠爱他们的养子。

