00:14:53.000 --> 00:15:51.000
James later stated, Those were the years when we were like, this is it, we're going to like our life. We both got good jobs, we were living real comfortable, we had everything we wanted. We go to church, we go to work, we pay our taxes and come home to our family. That's all you can ask for. In the early hours of Sunday, June 26, 2011, 911 received a call from a woman at Jackson's Metro Inn just off Highway 80. She had just witnessed a dark green Ford pickup truck run over a black man in the motel's parking lot. The perpetrators, who were identified as being young and white, were also heard hurling racial abuse at the victim.
詹姆斯后来表示：“那几年我们觉得，就是这样了，我们要喜欢我们的生活了。我们都有好工作，我们过得很舒服，我们拥有所需的一切。我们去教堂，去工作，我们纳税，然后回到家陪伴家人。这就是你所能奢求的一切。”2011年6月26日星期日凌晨，911接到了一名来自杰克逊80号公路旁地铁客栈的一名女性的电话。她刚刚目睹了一辆深绿色的福特皮卡在汽车旅馆的停车场撞倒了一名黑人男子。行凶者被确认是年轻的白人，人们还听到他们对受害者大声进行种族侮辱。

13
00:15:51.000 --> 00:17:05.000
When police arrived at the Metro Inn, they found several irate people gathered around a severely injured and unresponsive Craig Anderson on the curb of Ellis Avenue just outside the car park. Craig was rushed to hospital, but his injuries were severe and the situation dire. His attackers were divided between two vehicles, the Ford used in the hit and run, and a white Jeep SUV. Both cars were witnessed driving past the lot immediately after the attack, while their passengers pointed and laughed. Police sped onto the Interstate 20 where the Ford was last sighted travelling east and caught up to the vehicle. As they pulled up beside it, one officer locked eyes with the driver, a young white man with blonde hair and blue eyes. The officer noted, he had this blank stare about him. It was chilling, like a cold-hearted look. I'll never forget that look.
当警察到达地铁客栈时，他们发现几名愤怒的人聚集在停车场外埃利斯大道马路牙子上一个受重伤且无反应的克雷格·安德森周围。克雷格被紧急送往医院，但他的伤势严重，情况危急。他的袭击者分散在两辆车里，一辆是肇事逃逸时使用的福特汽车，另一辆是白色的吉普SUV。据目击者称，袭击发生后，两辆车都立即开过停车场，车上的乘客一边指指点点一边大笑。警察加速驶上80号州际公路，福特车最后被目击向东行驶，并追上了这辆车。当他们将车停在它旁边时，一名警官与司机——一个金发蓝眼的年轻白人男子——四目相对。这名警官注意到：“他有一种茫然的凝视。这让人毛骨悚然，就像一种冷酷无情的眼神。我永远不会忘记那个眼神。”

