00:17:05.000 --> 00:18:37.000
The driver was ordered to pull over and provide his driver's license, which identified him as 19-year-old Daryl Deadman. There were two female passengers in his truck, 17-year-old Shelby Richards and 18-year-old Sarah Graves. All three teens acted like they had no idea why the police had pulled them over, with the Deadman's demeanour akin to someone on their way home after an uneventful day. Shelby Richards seemed to think the whole law deal was a joke, while Sarah Graves appeared uncomfortable, as though she was part of something she didn't want to be involved with. The police inspected the Ford's exterior and found blood and brain matter on the right side of the front bumper. Later that morning, James returned to the home he shared with Craig Anderson after finishing his graveyard shift at the Airplane Parts factory where he worked. He quickly discovered that his husband wasn't home, and the next thing he knew, police officers were knocking at the door. They revealed that Craig had been in an accident overnight, and when James asked to go see him, the officers informed him that it wouldn't be possible, as Craig had been killed.
司机被命令靠边停车并出示驾照，驾照显示他是19岁的达里尔·迪德曼。他的卡车里有两名女乘客，17岁的谢尔比·理查兹和18岁的萨拉·格雷夫斯。这三个青少年表现得好像完全不知道警察为什么要拦下他们，迪德曼的举止类似于某人在经历了一个平淡无奇的日子后在回家的路上。谢尔比·理查兹似乎认为整个执法过程是个笑话，而萨拉·格雷夫斯则显得很不自在，好像她是她不想参与的事情的一部分。警察检查了福特车的外观，在右侧前保险杠上发现了血迹和脑浆。那天早上晚些时候，詹姆斯在飞机零件厂上完夜班后，回到了他和克雷格·安德森共同的家。他很快发现他的丈夫不在家，接下来他所知道的就是警察在敲门。他们透露克雷格昨夜出了事故，当詹姆斯要求去见他时，警官告诉他那是不可能的，因为克雷格已经遇害了。

15
00:18:37.000 --> 00:19:51.000
Daryl Deadman, Shelby Richards and Sarah Graves were taken into custody and interviewed separately. Deadman told police that Craig Anderson had jumped in front of his truck, while Richards, who was Deadman's girlfriend, laughed when she was brought into the interview room. In contrast, Sarah Graves appeared in shock and was crying. Once she had settled, she detailed the lead-up to the incident. On the night of Saturday, June 25, Graves and several dozen other youths were celebrating a birthday in a field near the village of Puckett, around 30 miles southeast of Jackson. They engaged in underage drinking around a bonfire until the party reached its conclusion at 4.15am. Ten party-goers then made a plan to meet up at a gas station in Brandon, a predominantly white neighborhood on the outskirts of Jackson, where the majority of the youths lived. At the gas station, the group discussed going to Jackson, which was a short drive west.
达里尔·迪德曼、谢尔比·理查兹和萨拉·格雷夫斯被拘留并分别接受了讯问。迪德曼告诉警察，克雷格·安德森跳到了他的卡车前面，而作为迪德曼女友的理查兹被带进审讯室时笑了。相比之下，萨拉·格雷夫斯显得惊恐万状并在哭泣。平静下来后，她详细讲述了事件的导火索。6月25日星期六晚上，格雷夫斯和其他几十名年轻人正在杰克逊东南约30英里、普克特村附近的一个田野里庆祝生日。他们在篝火旁饮酒，直到派对在凌晨4点15分结束。随后，十名派对参与者计划在布兰登的一家加油站会合，布兰登是杰克逊郊区的一个主要由白人居住的社区，大多数年轻人住在那里。在加油站，这群人讨论去杰克逊，那里向西只需短途车程。

16
00:19:51.000 --> 00:21:02.000
Three party-goers called at a night and went home, while the remaining seven committed to the trip. 23-year-old William Montgomery drove 18-year-olds John Rice and John Blalak and 20-year-old Dylan Butler in his white Jeep Cherokee SUV. Daryl Deadman took Sarah Graves and Shelby Richards in his green Ford F-250 pickup truck. During the drive into Jackson, Deadman and the girls received a call from the Jeep occupants, informing them that they were parked in the lot next to the Metro Inn on Ellis Avenue. Sarah Graves claimed that when they arrived, Rice and Blalak were talking to a black man in the motel's car park. Deadman then confronted the man and the pair got into a physical altercation. After the fight, Deadman returned to the Ford and referred to the man using racist terminology. Graves told detectives,
三名派对参与者打了个招呼就回家了，而剩下的七人则承诺成行。23岁的威廉·蒙哥马利驾驶着他的白色吉普切诺基SUV，载着18岁的约翰·赖斯、约翰·布莱拉克和20岁的迪伦·巴特勒。达里尔·迪德曼开着他的绿色福特F-250皮卡，载着萨拉·格雷夫斯和谢尔比·理查兹。在驱车前往杰克逊的途中，迪德曼和女孩们接到吉普车乘客的电话，通知他们停在埃利斯大道地铁客栈旁边的停车场里。萨拉·格雷夫斯声称，当他们到达时，赖斯和布莱拉克正在汽车旅馆的停车场里与一名黑人男子交谈。随后，迪德曼与该男子对峙，两人发生了身体冲突。冲突结束后，迪德曼回到福特车上，并用种族歧视的词汇称呼这名男子。格雷夫斯告诉侦探：

17
00:21:02.000 --> 00:22:04.000
We started pulling out and the guy was walking towards us and Deadman just stepped on it. The guy slipped under the car and then I freaked out and I went into like a shock. I couldn't breathe. I couldn't say anything. I didn't know what to do. I was scared. Afterwards, Deadman called Montgomery to brag about what he had done. The two groups then reconvened at a nearby McDonald's restaurant where Deadman laughed as he surveyed the front bumper of his car. After six hours at the police station, Sarah Graves was released without charge, as was Shelby Richards. Graves was picked up by her mother, Mary, who later described her daughter as seeming scared to death. She had Sarah admitted into hospital believing that she was suicidal.
“我们开始倒车离开，那家伙朝我们走来，迪德曼就猛踩油门。那家伙滑到了车底下，然后我吓坏了，进入了一种休克状态。我喘不过气来。我什么也说不出来。我不知道该怎么办。我很害怕。”之后，迪德曼打电话给蒙哥马利，吹嘘他所做的事情。两组人随后在附近的一家麦当劳餐厅重新会合，迪德曼一边查看他汽车的前保险杠一边大笑。在警察局呆了六个小时后，萨拉·格雷夫斯被无罪释放，谢尔比·理查兹也是如此。格雷夫斯被她的母亲玛丽接走，玛丽后来形容她的女儿看起来吓得要死。她让萨拉住进了医院，因为她认为她有自杀倾向。

18
00:22:04.000 --> 00:23:35.000
In the meantime, a remorseless Daryl Deadman was formally charged with Craig Anderson's murder. He posted the required 15% of his $50,000 bond securing his release pending trial. Police obtained CCTV footage from a security camera that overlooked the Ellis Avenue entrance to the car park. Both offenders' vehicles were filmed entering the lot, though only the Ford remained in view. Although the physical assault on Craig Anderson occurred off camera, multiple figures could be seen moving in and out of frame between the fight and the two cars. Before leaving, one figure believed to be Daryl Deadman was captured punching a fist in the air and was overheard by a security guard yelling white power. Even though a tree partly obscured the area where Craig was run over, Deadman's Ford could be seen steering up onto the curb and behind the tree before rising up over something and back down again. One officer said, It sent chills just watching the CCTV. I couldn't believe it. They ran Craig Anderson down like a dog.
与此同时，毫无悔意的达里尔·迪德曼被正式指控谋杀克雷格·安德森。他支付了5万美元保释金所需的15%，从而获释等待审判。警察从俯瞰停车场埃利斯大道入口的安全摄像头获取了闭路电视录像。两个违法者的车辆都被拍到进入停车场，尽管只有福特车留在视野内。尽管对克雷格·安德森的身体攻击发生在镜头之外，但在打斗和两辆车之间，可以看到多个人影在画面内外移动。在离开之前，一个被认为是达里尔·迪德曼的人被拍到将拳头向空中挥舞，并被保安听到高喊“白人力量”。尽管一棵树部分挡住了克雷格被撞倒的区域，但可以看到迪德曼的福特车开上路牙并穿过树后，然后又从某物上方升起并落回。一名警官说：“看闭路电视简直让人毛骨悚然。我简直不敢相信。他们像对待狗一样把克雷格·安德森撞倒了。”

19
00:23:35.000 --> 00:24:37.000
Detectives soon learned that the assault was instigated by teenager John Rice. After arriving at the car park, Rice and fellow Jeep passenger John Blaylack had approached Craig as he tried to access his locked car. They pretended to help, only to turn on Craig once Daryl Deadman arrived. Rice, Blaylack and Deadman then confronted Craig together. Deadman referred to Craig using a racial slur and yelled, Get away from my truck. Rice threw the first punch before Deadman continued the attack. As a result, John Rice was also charged with Craig's murder. This charge was ultimately reduced to simple assault after Rice's attorney successfully argued that his client had left in the Jeep before the fatal hit-and-run took place.
侦探们很快得知，袭击是由少年约翰·赖斯煽动的。到达停车场后，赖斯和吉普车的同伴约翰·布莱拉克在克雷格试图打开锁着的车门时接近了他。他们假装帮忙，直到达里尔·迪德曼到达后才对克雷格下手。随后，赖斯、布莱拉克和迪德曼一起与克雷格对峙。迪德曼用种族歧视的词语称呼克雷格并大喊：“离我的卡车远点。”赖斯出了第一拳，随后迪德曼继续袭击。因此，约翰·赖斯也被指控谋杀克雷格。在赖斯的律师成功辩称他的客户端在致命的肇事逃逸发生之前已经乘坐吉普车离开后，这一指控最终被减轻为普通袭击。

20
00:24:37.000 --> 00:26:02.000
Rice paid his $5,000 bond and was released. The apparent race-based motive for Craig's murder developed further as the investigation continued. Sarah Graves had told detectives that Daryl Deadman was a racist as she had heard him once say that he can't stand black people. Furthermore, witnesses had overheard Deadman and others yelling racial abuse at Craig, refer to him in a derogatory manner, and chant the racist slogan White Power immediately after the attack. However, the youths involved remained tight-lipped when questioned about their interactions with Craig and their reasons for being in Jackson that night. John Rice's attorney claimed that the group had gone to Jackson to buy alcohol and not to harass or assault anyone. Despite these assertions, investigators sought to present the case as a hate crime, but there wasn't enough evidence for the district attorney to proceed down that path. News of Craig Anderson's murder outraged Jackson's black community, prompting them to reach out to civil rights attorney J.D. Owens II.
赖斯支付了5000美元的保释金并被释放。随着调查的继续，克雷格谋杀案中明显的种族动机进一步显现。萨拉·格雷夫斯曾告诉侦探，达里尔·迪德曼是个种族主义者，因为她曾听他说过他无法忍受黑人。此外，目击者听到迪德曼和其他人对克雷格大喊种族侮辱，用贬损的方式称呼他，并在袭击发生后高呼种族主义口号“白人力量”。然而，涉案的年轻人当被问及他们与克雷格的互动以及那天晚上在杰克逊的原因时，仍然守口如瓶。约翰·赖斯的一名律师声称，这群人去杰克逊是为了买酒，而不是骚扰或袭击任何人。尽管有这些断言，调查人员仍试图将此案作为仇恨犯罪提交，但证据不足，无法让地方检察官沿着这条路走下去。克雷格·安德森被谋杀的消息激怒了杰克逊的黑人社区，促使他们联系了民权律师J·D·欧文斯二世。

21
00:26:02.000 --> 00:27:27.000
Owens worked for the Southern Poverty Law Center, a not-for-profit organization known for taking legal action against white supremacists and other extremist groups. In an effort to establish that the crime was racially motivated, Owens hired a private investigator to conduct an independent inquiry into Craig's death. A middle-aged white male was tactically chosen for the task, as he would be able to circulate easily within the communities where the suspects lived. The PI discovered that the seven youths present for Craig's murder, along with several others, had visited Jackson on multiple occasions to conduct what they had called hunting. The process involved searching the city for vulnerable black people to harass and attack. The investigator also discovered that Daryl Deadman had relatives who belonged to white supremacist groups. J.D. Owens shared the findings with the FBI, and five days after Craig's murder, they opened an investigation of their own. They found out that a few weeks prior to Craig's death, Daryl Deadman had been robbed by a black man.
欧文斯为南方贫困法律中心工作，这是一个以对白人至上主义者和其他极端主义群体采取法律行动而闻名的非营利组织。为了确定该犯罪具有种族动机，欧文斯聘请了一名私家侦探对克雷格的死进行独立调查。一名中年的白人男性被战术性地挑选来执行这项任务，因为他能够轻松地在嫌疑人居住的社区中活动。这名私家侦探发现，出席克雷格谋杀案的七名年轻人以及其他几人曾多次访问杰克逊，进行他们所谓的“狩猎”。这个过程包括在城市中搜寻脆弱的黑人进行骚扰和袭击。调查人员还发现，达里尔·迪德曼有属于白人至上主义团体的亲属。J·D·欧文斯将这些发现分享给了联邦调查局，在克雷格遇害五天后，他们展开了自己的调查。他们发现，在克雷格死前几周，达里尔·迪德曼曾被一名黑人男子抢劫。

22
00:27:27.000 --> 00:28:53.000
This supported the belief that the hit-and-run had been an intentional act by Deadman, likely motivated by revenge. Craig Anderson's funeral was held six days after his death at his former parish, the first-hired Park Baptist Church. As requested by the Anderson family, the service focused on celebrating Craig's life rather than the brutal nature of his death, and there was no mention of hate or anger. Craig's sister, Barbara, spoke of her brother's love for cooking, his sense of fashion, and his humour. She called his death untimely, and chose not to speak out against those responsible. Pastor Brian Richardson and his 17-year-old son, Jordan, were two of the few white people in attendance. Jordan attended Brandon High School with Daryl Deadman and had endured two years of violent bullying at his hands, partly because he had black friends. Earlier that year, Deadman had been arrested and convicted of misdemeanor harassment against Jordan and was on probation at the time of Craig's murder.
这支持了肇事逃逸是迪德曼的蓄意行为这一信念，很可能是出于报复动机。克雷格·安德森的葬礼在他去世六天后在他以前的教区——第一受雇公园浸信会教堂举行。正如安德森家族所要求的，礼拜的重点是庆祝克雷格的一生，而不是他死去的残酷性质，并且没有提及仇恨或愤怒。克雷格的姐姐芭芭拉谈到了她的弟弟对烹饪的热爱、他的时尚感和他的幽默感。她称他的死是不合时宜的，并选择不对那些负有责任的人大声指责。牧师布莱恩·理查森和他的17岁儿子乔丹是仅有的几名出席的白人之一。乔丹与达里尔·迪德曼一起在布兰登高中上学，并忍受了他长达两年的暴力欺凌，部分原因是他有黑人朋友。今年早些时候，迪德曼因对乔丹进行轻罪骚扰而被捕并定罪，在克雷格被谋杀时正处于缓刑期。

23
00:28:53.000 --> 00:30:17.000
On July 6, 2011, Daryl Deadman was called back to court for a bond revocation hearing. The prosecution were now confidently calling the murder of Craig Anderson a hate crime. After presenting the evidence that supported their position, the prosecution put forward that Deadman had left the party in the early hours of June 26 with the intention of going in search of a black person to attack. Deadman's attorney rejected these allegations, but the judge was satisfied with the evidence presented and a Deadman's bond was increased from $50,000 to $800,000. Unable to secure the payment, Deadman was placed in police custody to await trial. By this stage, the CCTV footage from the Metro Inn parking lot had been leaked to the press and broadcast on televised news reports throughout the country. As a result, Deadman was isolated in jail for his own safety. Meanwhile, the assistant police chief told CNN reporters that Craig's death was an isolated incident and denied that the attack was part of a bigger story.
2011年7月6日，达里尔·迪德曼被传唤回法庭参加保释撤销听证会。控方现在有信心地称克雷格·安德森的谋杀案为仇恨犯罪。在出示支持其立场的证据后，控方提出迪德曼在6月26日凌晨离开派对，意图寻找一名黑人进行袭击。迪德曼的律师驳回了这些指控，但法官对提交的证据感到满意，迪德曼的保释金从5万美元增加到80万美元。由于无法筹集这笔款项，迪德曼被置于警察拘留中等待审判。此时，地铁客栈停车场的闭路电视录像已被泄露给媒体，并在全国各地的电视新闻报道中播出。因此，为了他自身的安全，迪德曼在监狱中被隔离。与此同时，助理警察局长告诉CNN记者，克雷格的死是一起孤立事件，并否认这次袭击是更大故事的一部分。

24
00:30:17.000 --> 00:31:53.000
CNN also spoke with the Jordan Richardson, the teenager Deadman had been previously convicted of harassing. Jordan said that Deadman always had a look of no conscience and carried around this backpack of hatred. Jordan's father, Pastor Brian Richardson, told CNN he had warned his son about Deadman's volatility and had been worried that Deadman might go as far as to kill Jordan. Pastor Richardson had told the police it was painfully clear that Deadman was going to injure someone severely or possibly kill someone. Other Brandon High School students told CNN that Deadman and his friends bullied white classmates who had black friends and used the racist language in real life and online. He had protested at school when Barack Obama was elected America's first African American president and referred to him using racist insults on social media. According to the students, school administrators mostly looked the other way as the racial hatred and bullying intensified. When CNN contacted Brandon High administrators, a spokesperson told them that the school took bullying very seriously and had no record of any incidents involving Deadman.
CNN还采访了乔丹·理查森，这个迪德曼先前被判骚扰的青少年。乔丹说，迪德曼总是有一种没有良心的表情，随身带着这个充满仇恨的背包。乔丹的父亲，布莱恩·理查森牧师告诉CNN，他曾警告过他的儿子迪德曼的反复无常，并一直担心迪德曼可能会走得太远而杀死乔丹。理查森牧师曾告诉警察，很痛心地清楚迪德曼会严重伤害某人或可能杀死某人。布兰登高中的其他学生告诉CNN，迪德曼和他的朋友们欺凌有黑人朋友的白人同学，在现实生活和网上使用种族主义语言。当巴拉克·奥巴马当选为美国第一位非裔美国总统时，他在学校抗议，并在社交媒体上用种族主义侮辱来称呼他。据学生们说，随着种族仇恨和欺凌的加剧，学校管理人员大多视而不见。当CNN联系布兰登高中的管理人员时，一位发言人告诉他们，学校非常重视欺凌行为，并且没有任何涉及迪德曼的事件记录。

25
00:31:53.000 --> 00:33:02.000
A former friend revealed that Deadman and his group were referred to as the Brandon Boys and were known for going out at night to target black individuals. Ken Johnson, the manager of a service station in Brandon where Deadman and his friends often hung out, told CNN. That seemed like every word that came out of their mouth was the N word. Ken once told the group to mind their behavior after he overheard them say that black people were taking over their town. Ken told CNN. Deadman made it well known that he didn't like a gay or black people. He talked about Jackson being a predominantly black city and said his parents grew up and moved away because of all these black people. Many Brandon locals were outraged that their town was being accused of racism and told reporters that they didn't view Craig Anderson's death as a hate crime.
一位前朋友透露，迪德曼和他的团伙被称为“布兰登男孩”，并以夜间出动针对黑人个人而闻名。肯·约翰逊是布兰登一家服务站的经理，迪德曼和他的朋友经常在那里闲逛，他告诉CNN：“似乎他们嘴里说出的每一个字都是N字。”肯曾有一次告诉这群人注意他们的行为，因为他无意中听到他们说黑人正在接管他们的镇子。肯告诉CNN：“迪德曼让人清楚地知道他不喜欢同性恋或黑人。他谈到杰克逊是一个以黑人为主的城市，并说他的父母因为所有这些黑人而长大并搬走了。”许多布兰登当地人对他们的城镇被指控为种族主义感到愤怒，并告诉记者他们不认为克雷格·安德森的死是一起仇恨犯罪。

26
00:33:02.000 --> 00:34:54.000
While they agreed that Deadman had violated the law, they didn't believe he had targeted Craig because of his race. A white senior from Brandon High told the Jackson Free Press that the residents of Brandon were very down to worth and that she was worried Craig's death would reflect poorly on them. Quote, Brandon is one of the top places to live in the country. There is nothing bad about Brandon. It's a shame the crime happened. Deadman's younger sister told The New York Times, we're just country and whoever comes here, we welcome everybody. This whole thing is getting blown out of proportion. Deadman's uncle described his nephew as a good boy from a happy-go-lucky family who got involved with the wrong crowd. A relative of John Rice, Deadman's co-accused, took to Facebook to say that Rice wasn't a murderer but had fallen victim to trial by media and was suffering from, quote, reverse racism. Another Facebook user echoed this sentiment, writing, if this was the other way around and a black guy ran over a white boy, it would not be a hate crime. Baseless rumors spread around Brandon that Craig's death was drug-related, prompting Michael Teasley, the white president of Jackson State University's chapter of the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People, to speak out.
虽然他们同意迪德曼违反了法律，但他们不认为他因为克雷格的种族而将其作为目标。布兰登高中的一名白人高年级学生告诉《杰克逊自由报》，布兰登的居民非常脚踏实地，她担心克雷格的死会给他们带来不好的反映。“引文：布兰登是全国最适合居住的地方之一。布兰登没有任何不好的地方。发生这起犯罪真是一个遗憾。”迪德曼的妹妹告诉《纽约时报》：“我们只是乡下人，无论谁来这里，我们都欢迎所有人。这整件事被夸大了。”迪德曼的叔叔将他的侄女婿描述为一个来自快乐家庭的好男孩，却误交了损友。迪德曼的同案被告约翰·赖的一位亲属在Facebook上发帖称，赖斯不是杀人犯，而是沦为了舆论审判的受害者，并遭受了“引文：反向种族主义”。另一位Facebook用户也呼应了这种情绪，写道：“如果情况反过来，一个黑人撞死了一个白男孩，这就不会是一次仇恨犯罪。”关于克雷格的死与毒品有关的毫无根据的谣言在布兰登流传，促使全国有色人种协进会杰克逊州立大学分会白人主席迈克尔·蒂斯利大声疾呼。

27
00:34:54.000 --> 00:36:56.000
Michael, who was a reformed racist himself, stated, it's much easier for Rankin County to blame the black man than take responsibility for this crime. Right now, the problem is in their churches, homes, and schools. This doesn't have anything to do with a drug deal gone bad. They are looking for an excuse to make themselves feel better. Gerald Rose, founder of the New Order National Human Rights Organization, said that the situation could be used to provoke level-headed discussions about race relations, quote, When I saw the video, I shed tears. That could have been me, or it could have been my sons. We want to call for a healing process, and at the same time, we are aware racism is still alive. I can't believe stuff like this is going on in the year 2011. On August 14, 2011, more than 500 people, including clergymen, elected officials, and supporters of all races, gathered at the New Horizon Church in Jackson to march against racial injustice. T-shirts were distributed amongst the protesters, printed with the slogan, Not in My City. They marched through Jackson singing, We Shall Overcome, and This Little Light of Mine, before gathering in the Metro Wing Car Park for a candlelight vigil. Rabbi Valerie Cohen told the attendees, We are here to unify and to teach ourselves and our children, and everyone out there, that love is a better way to live. We are here to get beyond hatred.
迈克尔曾经是一个改过自新的种族主义者，他表示：“兰金县更容易把责任推卸给黑人，而不是为这起犯罪承担责任。现在，问题出在他们的教堂、家庭和学校里。这与毒品交易变坏没有任何关系。他们只是在寻找借口让自己感觉好一点。”新秩序人权组织创始人杰拉尔德·罗斯表示，这种情况可以用来引发关于种族关系的冷静讨论，“引文：当我看到这段视频时，我流下了眼泪。那可能是我，或者可能是我的儿子们。我们想要呼吁一个治愈的过程，与此同时，我们意识到种族主义仍然活着。我简直不敢相信在2011年还会发生这样的事情。”2011年8月14日，包括神职人员、民选官员和各族支持者在内的500多人聚集在杰克逊的新地平线教堂，游行抗议种族不平等。抗议者分发了印有“不在我的城市”口号的T恤。他们唱着“我们一定会克服”和“我这小小的光芒”穿过杰克逊游行，然后聚集在地铁客栈停车场举行烛光守夜活动。拉比瓦莱里·科恩对出席者说：“我们在这里是为了团结，并教导我们自己和我们的孩子，以及那里的每个人，爱是更好的生活方式。我们在这里是为了超越仇恨。”

28
00:36:56.000 --> 00:38:38.000
Craig's husband, to James, was in too much emotional pain to attend the vigil. He told Buzzfeed News that following the murder, he had purchased a gun in fear that Craig's attackers would also come for him. He blamed himself for not being with Craig on the night he was killed, saying, I should have been there. I always protected him. That was my job. James lost his faith and stopped going to church and to work, instead spending his days crying in bed with the lights off and the curtains drawn. As a result, the couple's four-year-old adopted son went to live with the James's mother. James avoided the news as he didn't want to see the CCTV footage of Craig's death. One afternoon, James was driving his adopted son to his mother's house when he said, You can't go that way. That's where dead men killed Craig. Stunned, James looked around and realized that they were passing the Metro Wing car park. He asked his son how he knew what happened there, to which the child responded, I saw it on TV. Almost two months after Craig Anderson's death, Daryl Deadman's murder charge was upgraded to capital murder.
克雷格的丈夫詹姆斯因悲痛欲绝而无法出席守夜活动。他告诉《BuzzFeed新闻》，谋杀案发生后，他买了一把枪，因为害怕克雷格的袭击者也会来找他。他责备自己在克雷格被杀的那晚没有陪在他身边，并说：“我本应该在那里的。我总是保护他。那是我的工作。”詹姆斯失去了信仰，不再去教堂和上班，而是在拉上窗帘、关着灯的床上哭泣度日。结果，这对夫妇4岁的养子去和詹姆斯的母亲住在一起。詹姆斯避开新闻，因为他不想看到克雷格死时的闭路电视画面。一天下午，詹姆斯正开车载着他的养子去他母亲家，这时养子说：“你不能走那条路。那是死人杀死克雷格的地方。”惊呆了的詹姆斯环顾四周，意识到他们正路过地铁客栈停车场。他问他的儿子怎么知道那里发生了什么，对此孩子回答说：“我在电视上看到了。”在克雷格·安德森死后近两个月，达里尔·迪德曼的谋杀罪名被升级为谋杀罪。

